---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/v2/BaseLayout.astro';
import NewsletterBlock from '../../../components/v2/NewsletterBlock.astro';
import { routeSlug, titleize, placeLabel, typeLabel } from '../../../lib/editorial';

const allVenues = await getCollection('venues');
const slugs = ['polperro-villas','point-leo-estate-villas','jackalope','lindenderry','peninsula-hot-springs-glamping','hotel-sorrento','the-continental-sorrento'];
const venues = slugs.map((slug) => allVenues.find((venue) => routeSlug(venue) === slug)).filter((venue): venue is NonNullable<typeof venue> => Boolean(venue));

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/')
  ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL
  : import.meta.env.BASE_URL + '/';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Couples Accommodation Mornington Peninsula · Peninsula Insider"
  description="The best couples accommodation on the Mornington Peninsula, from vineyard villas and design hotels to slower coastal stays built for two."
  section="stay"
>

<section class="hero" aria-label="Couples Accommodation on the Mornington Peninsula">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="hero__frame">
      <div class="hero__above">
        <div class="hero__meta">
          <a href={`${base}stay/`} class="hero__meta-tag" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;">Stay</a>
          <span class="hero__meta-divider"></span>
          <span class="hero__meta-date">For two <span class="ornament">—</span> {new Date().getFullYear()}</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="hero__headline">Couples accommodation on the <em>Mornington Peninsula</em>.</h1>
        <p class="hero__dek">The right Peninsula stay for two should do more than look good in a booking thumbnail. It should give the weekend shape.</p>
        <div class="hero__byline">
          <span>— By <strong>The Peninsula Insider Editors</strong></span>
          <a href="#rankings" class="hero__byline-read">Jump to the list <span style="opacity:.5;margin-left:.3rem;">{venues.length} stays</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure>
        <img class="hero__image" src={`${base}images/sourced/place-red-hill-01.webp`} alt="Red Hill vineyard weekends" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high">
        <figcaption class="hero__image-cap">
          <span>Red Hill <span class="ornament">—</span> the couples' version of wine country</span>
          <span>Photography <span class="ornament">/</span> The Insider</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="letter" aria-labelledby="methodology-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="letter__frame">
      <div class="letter__body">
        <div class="letter__eyebrow">
          <span class="letter__eyebrow-rule"></span>
          <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--ochre">Editor's Note</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="letter__head" id="methodology-title">Four <em>modes</em> for two.</h2>
        <div class="letter__prose">
          <p>The right Peninsula stay for two should do more than look good in a booking thumbnail. It should give the weekend shape. That usually means one of four things: vineyard quiet, coastal village access, thermal-springs atmosphere, or a design-led hotel that makes the staying itself part of the point.</p>
          <p>The strongest couples stays on the Peninsula tend to be slower rather than louder. Polperro Villas, Point Leo Estate Villas, and Lindenderry work best when the weekend is built around wine, long lunches, and a late breakfast. Jackalope is sharper and more performative. Peninsula Hot Springs Glamping is the most obviously experience-led option. Hotel Sorrento and The Continental make more sense when the trip needs the village and the coast as much as the room.</p>
          <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--soft)">Last fact-verified: 24 April 2026</p>
        </div>
        <div class="letter__sig">
          <span class="letter__sig-mark">—</span>
          <div>
            <div class="letter__sig-name">The Editors</div>
            <div class="letter__sig-role">Peninsula Insider</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="letter__side">
        <img class="letter__image" src={`${base}images/sourced/place-sorrento-01.webp`} alt="Sorrento village">
        <figcaption class="letter__image-cap">Sorrento main street <em>— the coastal version.</em></figcaption>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="shortlist" id="rankings" aria-labelledby="shortlist-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="shortlist__frame">
      <div class="shortlist__intro">
        <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--ochre">The Shortlist</span>
        <h2 id="shortlist-title">{venues.length} stays that make the strongest Peninsula <em>couples weekend</em>.</h2>
        <p class="shortlist__intro-body">Vineyard stays, design hotels, thermal glamping, and coastal bases that give the trip the right pace.</p>
        <a href={`${base}stay/`} class="shortlist__intro-link">All Peninsula stays
          <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M5 12h14m-5-5 5 5-5 5"/></svg>
        </a>
      </div>
      <ol class="shortlist__list" style="list-style:none;">
        {venues.map((v, i) => {
          const data = v.data;
          const hats = data.authority?.hats ?? 0;
          const num = String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0');
          const place = placeLabel(data.place);
          const type = typeLabel[data.type] ?? data.type;
          const allTags = [
            ...(data.tags?.mood ?? []),
            ...(data.tags?.audience ?? []),
          ].slice(0, 3);
          return (
            <li class="sl-item">
              <span class="sl-item__num">{num}</span>
              <div class="sl-item__body">
                <div class="sl-item__meta">
                  <span>{place}</span>
                  <span class="sl-item__meta-sep"></span>
                  <span>{type}</span>
                  <span class="sl-item__meta-sep"></span>
                  <span>{data.priceBand}</span>
                </div>
                <a href={`${base}stay/${routeSlug(v)}/`} class="sl-item__name">{data.name}</a>
                <p class="sl-item__why">{data.signature}</p>
                <div class="sl-item__tags">
                  {hats > 0 && <span class="sl-item__tag sl-item__tag--hat">{hats} hat{hats > 1 ? 's' : ''}</span>}
                  {allTags.map((tag: string) => (
                    <span class="sl-item__tag">{titleize(tag)}</span>
                  ))}
                </div>
              </div>
            </li>
          );
        })}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="letter" aria-labelledby="guide-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="letter__frame" style="display:block;">
      <div class="letter__body">
        <div class="letter__eyebrow">
          <span class="letter__eyebrow-rule"></span>
          <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--ochre">Editorial Guide</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="letter__head" id="guide-title">Editorial <em>guide</em>.</h2>
        <div class="letter__prose">
          <p><strong>Most romantic?</strong><br>Polperro Villas and Point Leo Estate Villas are the strongest if intimacy and setting matter most. Jackalope is the more dramatic answer.</p>
          <p><strong>Best for a food-and-wine weekend?</strong><br>Lindenderry, Jackalope, and Polperro Villas all sit inside the strongest Peninsula appetite zone.</p>
          <p><strong>Best for coast plus village?</strong><br>Hotel Sorrento and The Continental are the right answer when the weekend is supposed to include walking, bay-and-ocean access, and dinner without a long drive home.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<NewsletterBlock />
</BaseLayout>
